      "writtenOn": "2019-12-13T21:01:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about instead using something like:\n\nPLATFORM_SDK_VERSION\u003d$(OUT_DIR\u003d${OUT_DIR}/get_build_var/ get_build_var PLATFORM_SDK_VERSION)\n\nThat way we can build into out/ instead of out-aml/ which can affect the binary contents, since paths to generated files can end up in at least the debug info.",
      "revId": "41ce667f7c881876af14467a84c1ec5000af5090",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "900e1877_878e0973",
        "filename": "scripts/build-aml-prebuilts.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-16T22:32:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If out/ already exists and contains a normal lunch target build then this script will still fail in \"m --skip-make\" below. For normal developer use it\u0027d be confusing and inconvenient to either have to delete their normal out/ first, or get the habit to always do \"env OUT_DIR\u003dout-aml/ build-aml-prebuilts.sh\".\n\nI think rather we should fix the build system to properly handle both normal and skip-make builds in the same tree. Maybe it\u0027s just a matter of using two different ninja files (e.g. out/soong/build.ninja and out/soong/build-skip-make.ninja), maybe more work is necessary. That\u0027s not something I\u0027ve looked into.\n\nBarring that, if bogus out-aml/ paths turns out to be a problem in prod builds we can instead wrap this script in \"env OUT_DIR\u003dout/get_build_var AML_PREBUILTS_OUT_DIR\u003dout ...\" there.",
      "parentUuid": "a7d3418e_4efa93e4",
      "revId": "41ce667f7c881876af14467a84c1ec5000af5090",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
