      "message": "\u003e Maybe rm $OUT_DIR/.soong_in_make?\n\n(I assume you mean $OUT_DIR/soong/.soong.in_make.) It\u0027d still mean that a user switching between normal lunch builds and build-aml-prebuilts.sh would have a worse incremental build experience than with different out dirs, wouldn\u0027t it?\n\n\u003e That can be a future change though.\n\nGood, thanks. I suppose we could live with the churn in the same out dir if it\u0027s restricted to rerunning Soong and Kati, but I\u0027d then document a \"pro-tip\" to set OUT_DIR to something else for interactive use.\n\nFWIW I changed the logic here a bit to only fall back to out-aml if OUT_DIR exists and has .soong.in_make, so in a prod build with its own target it\u0027d use out/.",
